[00:37.56]M: Do you mind taking my photo with the statue over there?
[00:40.50]M: I think it will make a great shot.
[00:42.62]W: Sure, no worries.
[00:44.06]W: You're always taking photos.
[00:46.12]W: What do you do with all the photos you take?
[00:48.94]M: Well, don't laugh.
[00:50.36]M: My dream is to become an online celebrity of sorts.
[00:54.12]W: You are not serious, are you?
[00:55.50]M: I am, completely.
[00:57.78]M: I just got the idea a few months ago after posting some holiday photos on my social media accounts.
[01:04.40]M: A lot of people liked my photos and started asking me for travel tips.
[01:08.86]M: So I figured I'd give it a go.
[01:11.56]M: I post a lot on social media anyway.
[01:14.14]M: So I've got nothing to lose.
[01:16.16]W: I guess that's true.
[01:17.96]W: So what do you have to do to become Internet famous?
[01:22.04]M: Surprisingly a lot more than I did as a hobby.
[01:25.80]M: Recently, I've been spending a lot more time editing photos, posting online and clearing storage on my phone.
[01:32.56]M: It's always full now.
[01:34.32]W: That doesn't sound like too much work.
[01:36.98]M: Well, there's more to it.
[01:38.64]M: I spent all last weekend researching what topics are popular, what words to use in captions and similar accounts to follow.
[01:46.86]M: It really was a lot to take in.
[01:48.56]M: And I was up well past midnight.
[01:51.92]M: I'd say it's paying off though.
[01:54.06]M: I increased the number of people following my accounts by 15% already.
[01:58.44]W: That is impressive.
[02:00.20]W: I guess I never thought much about all the effort behind the scene.
[02:04.92]W: Now that I think about it, there's always something wrong with my photos as it is—half smiles, closed eyes, messy hair.
[02:14.02]W: I hope you have better luck than I do.
[02:16.54]W: Then again, I think the only person interested in my photos is my mom.
